// Renode platform override for ATSAME70Q20B. Renode upstream ships
// platforms/cpus/sam_e70.repl with CPU + NVIC + USART0/1/2 + PMC_SR
// flipflop + a CIDR Tag + ApplySVD, but is missing three pieces
// klipper firmware needs:
//
//   1. DWT - klipper's generic ARM Cortex-M timer (src/generic/
//      armcm_timer.c) reads DWT->CYCCNT as the system clock. Without
//      a DWT model the register reads zero forever, so timer_read_time
//      returns 0 and the klippy handshake never advances.
//
//   2. UART2 - klipper's SAME70 host link in CONFIG_ATSAM_SERIAL mode
//      is UART2 (PD25/PD26) per src/atsam/serial.c. The upstream repl
//      exposes USART0..2 only and Atmel UART is a separate peripheral
//      block; we add it at datasheet base 0x400E1A00 with UART2_IRQn=44
//      (SAME70Q20B datasheet / lib/same70b/include/same70q20b.h).
//
//   3. USBHS - klipper's SAME70 host link in CONFIG_ATSAM_USB mode
//      runs through the chip's USB High-Speed device controller (the
//      duet3-6hc / duet3-6xd printer configs are USB+CAN-only and have
//      no serial-mode firmware variant). Renode upstream has no SAM
//      USB-OTG / USBHS peripheral model, so we ship a local one in
//      test/emulator/repl/same70_usbhs.cs (loaded via `i @<file>`
//      emitted by renode_launcher._render_resc before this .repl is
//      parsed). The model uses a "skip-enum cheat" - inject a single
//      SET_CONFIGURATION SETUP packet on EP0 so klipper's CDC stack
//      reaches the bulk-active state without a full enumeration walk
//      - then exposes BULK_IN/BULK_OUT as a UART pipe via UARTBase so
//      UartPtyTerminal can connect to it the same way it does to
//      uart2 in the serial-mode build.
//
// The flash size in upstream sam_e70.repl is sized 0x10000000 (way
// oversized vs the actual 1MB), which is harmless - LoadELF only
// touches the bytes the firmware uses.
//
// AFEC0/AFEC1 stubbing happens at runtime via afec_stub.py rather
// than in this .repl - see _AFEC_BASES_FOR_CHIP / afec_block in
// renode_launcher.py. Doing it that way keeps the per-instance file
// path resolved by the launcher (rather than baked into the .repl)
// so checkouts at different filesystem locations both work.
using "platforms/cpus/sam_e70.repl"

dwt: Miscellaneous.DWT @ sysbus 0xE0001000
    frequency: 300000000

uart2: UART.SAM_USART @ sysbus 0x400E1A00
    uartOnlyMode: true
    enablePdc: true
    ->nvic@44

usbhs: USB.SAM_USBHS @ {
        sysbus 0x40038000;
        sysbus new Bus.BusMultiRegistration { address: 0xa0100000; size: 0x80000; region: "fifo" }
    }
    IRQ -> nvic@34
